  "details": "Me and my roommate, on the same internet. Half gigabit fiberoptics crashed 3 times, where atleast 1 was at exact same time. Could be a home network issue, but have ruled this unlikely. We are both hooked up to the interwebs via Gigabit ethernet (Cat6) Roomate Via a switch (connected to her computer and main router by CAT6), and me via a Wireless Access point, connected to computer and main router via CAT6. \nWe both crashed at exactly the same time, with message \"VRchat not responding\" it did not say \"connection time out\". \nThat is why i am reporting this as a bug, i am unable to find a problem in my home network setup.",
